{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1393774-belial-s-brood-and-gaining-willpower","id":1393774,"title":"Belial's Brood and gaining Willpower","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-03T06:51:04-07:00","id":1393774,"title":"Belial's Brood and gaining Willpower","content":"Don't have Spilled Blood, but been reading comments about the new Brood. Loved the old one and am curious how they've been adapted to 2E. Anyway, as I understand it, they have no Touchstones, Mask or Dirge, and thus seem unable to gain Willpower if used as PCs.<br /> <br /> However, I came across something in the CoD rule book that makes sense for them: if you score an exceptional success using Down and Dirty combat, you get a Willpower back. This seems like it would be in theme with the Brood. Go pick nasty fights after depleting your Willpower to replenish it. Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11149-pj123","name":"PJ123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T07:21:30-07:00","id":1393777,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1367266-spilled-blood-on-dtrpg?p=1368435#post1368435\">As vampires</a>, the Brood have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1271662-how-wells-a-predatory-elder-work-for-a-session?p=1271678#post1271678\">a particular form of resource-farming</a> available to them by virtue of <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/foru